WEBVTT

01:17.243 --> 01:20.080
THE TRUNK

01:21.831 --> 01:25.043
5 MONTHS AGO

01:55.782 --> 01:57.075
What did he…

01:58.409 --> 02:00.620
"I lived a good life, thanks to you."

02:13.424 --> 02:14.968
He's gone. I'm sorry.

02:16.970 --> 02:18.138
3:10 p.m.

02:20.598 --> 02:23.184
Uh, that'd be 15…

02:23.268 --> 02:25.019
It's fine. I already announced it.

02:28.356 --> 02:30.441
I'm deeply sorry
for your loss, ma'am.

02:30.942 --> 02:33.069
Would you contact his next of kin, please?

02:38.324 --> 02:41.870
But aren't you his wife?
Where are you going?

02:43.746 --> 02:45.874
I'm not his wife anymore. He's dead now.

03:43.640 --> 03:46.768
PROCEED TO YOUR NEXT MARRIAGE?
YES OR NO

04:03.618 --> 04:06.037
Hello, Ms. Noh.
Hope you enjoyed your assignment.

04:15.171 --> 04:17.590
DIVORCE CONFIRMATION

04:17.674 --> 04:20.551
FIELD WIFE TASK COMPLETION REPORT
NOH IN-JI

04:21.844 --> 04:24.889
So, Deputy Manager Noh,
how was your marriage this time?

04:24.973 --> 04:25.807
NOH IN-JI

04:27.684 --> 04:29.394
I'm sure you could use a vacation.

04:30.395 --> 04:32.188
I'm ready for another assignment.

04:33.690 --> 04:34.524
Okay.

04:42.615 --> 04:44.993
This one is not
a match made in heaven, Ms. Noh.

04:47.787 --> 04:50.748
It's going to be very different
from your other marriages.

04:59.924 --> 05:01.718
NM MEMBER PROFILE
HAN JEONG-WON

05:01.801 --> 05:04.637
I heard that prick Han Jeong-won
is writing movie scores.

05:05.263 --> 05:07.140
He's supposed to be running the company.

05:07.223 --> 05:08.891
Dude is asleep at the wheel.

05:08.975 --> 05:11.394
I saw him earlier,
blitzed out of his mind.

05:11.477 --> 05:13.604
Probably getting
high as a kite, man.

05:13.688 --> 05:14.689
No shit.

05:15.189 --> 05:17.317
Man, I coulda told you that. Wait.

05:17.984 --> 05:20.278
You think that's why he got divorced?
'Cause of the drugs?

05:20.361 --> 05:21.904
How the fuck would I know?

05:21.988 --> 05:23.990
Hey, tell me what you heard. I wanna know!

05:24.073 --> 05:24.907
I don't know!

05:24.991 --> 05:26.868
Come on.
You know something, so spill it.

05:26.951 --> 05:28.328
Man, just shut up!

07:32.827 --> 07:35.079
The number you have dialed
is not available.

07:35.163 --> 07:36.706
At the tone, please record your message.

07:36.789 --> 07:37.957
WIFE

07:38.040 --> 07:40.042
Taking sleeping pills
in the bathroom again?

07:40.543 --> 07:42.086
What are you, a zombie?

07:42.170 --> 07:44.297
Who the hell does that at a club anyway?

07:44.380 --> 07:47.175
Word on the street is
you're turning into a pill-popper.

07:47.258 --> 07:48.092
So what's up?

07:48.176 --> 07:51.095
Why are you dicking around at a club
when you could be at home in bed?

07:51.179 --> 07:52.638
I can't sleep at home.

07:52.722 --> 07:54.765
That makes no sense. Your house is huge.

07:54.849 --> 07:56.225
You tried hopping between rooms?

07:56.309 --> 07:58.478
I'm sure you'll find one
that gets the job done.

07:58.561 --> 08:01.439
This is what's wrong with rich guys.
You wanna be cavalier and independent.

08:01.522 --> 08:02.398
Go to a hospital!

08:02.482 --> 08:04.484
I've been going to one for 20 years, dude.

08:05.026 --> 08:07.487
They're about to write me a prescription,
actually. See ya.

08:21.667 --> 08:24.045
The number you have dialed
is not available.

08:56.869 --> 08:57.828
WIFE

08:59.956 --> 09:02.500
Please take down that chandelier thing.
It's hideous.

09:03.000 --> 09:05.086
It's not a chandelier.
It's a work of art.

09:05.169 --> 09:06.879
Besides, your dad loved that thing.

09:07.713 --> 09:09.173
That's why I don't want it.

09:10.508 --> 09:12.510
We can't just hang anything up there.

09:13.511 --> 09:17.139
I'm looking for a different piece
in France, so hold off. Leave it alone.

11:33.901 --> 11:35.111
Han Jeong-won.

11:38.656 --> 11:39.990
It's been a while, huh?

11:46.997 --> 11:49.166
Oh, uh, I've found that
it tends to put people at ease

11:49.250 --> 11:50.876
if I approach them like this.

11:51.502 --> 11:53.170
You don't have to play ball, you know.

11:53.254 --> 11:56.090
Then again,
you probably don't wanna catch a warrant.

11:56.173 --> 11:57.591
That, uh, wouldn't be fun.

11:58.426 --> 11:59.593
All right, who was it?

12:00.302 --> 12:01.637
You know Jay Yoong, right?

12:02.221 --> 12:04.557
It was Yoong, wasn't it? Or was it Young?

12:05.725 --> 12:06.684
Mm.

12:07.393 --> 12:10.438
Last night at the club,
Mr. Jay, uh… uh, whatever,

12:10.521 --> 12:11.772
was taken into custody.

12:11.856 --> 12:13.107
Caught red-handed.

12:13.190 --> 12:14.900
And you were hanging out there.

12:17.194 --> 12:19.780
Look at that. Thank you very much.

12:21.407 --> 12:23.576
- Okay. Here.
- Why do you pick on me so much?

12:23.659 --> 12:25.035
Why?

12:25.619 --> 12:27.663
You're loaded from selling
all those shares.

12:27.747 --> 12:30.291
You got plenty of free time.
Oh, and your history.

12:30.374 --> 12:32.877
"History"? I was just a kid. Come on.

12:35.463 --> 12:37.423
Seventeen basically makes you an adult.

12:38.007 --> 12:40.718
You knew it was wrong.
You knew the consequences.

12:58.819 --> 13:00.112
- Piece of shit.
- Whoa!

13:00.196 --> 13:01.363
Whoa! Hey, hey, stop!

13:01.447 --> 13:04.116
- Hyung, Hyung, Hyung, Hyung, Hyung.
- You son of a bitch!

13:04.200 --> 13:06.243
- What the hell?
- Get the hell off me!

13:07.912 --> 13:08.871
Stop!

13:09.455 --> 13:10.956
- You piece of shit!
- Relax!

13:11.040 --> 13:13.459
- You son of a bitch!
- Stop! What the--

13:13.542 --> 13:15.169
Bastard! Get back here!

13:16.712 --> 13:18.464
Look, he ratted me out, dude!

13:19.256 --> 13:20.591
Just take it.

13:20.674 --> 13:21.634
The whole thing.

13:21.717 --> 13:23.469
You could buy me out.
Run the place yourself.

13:23.552 --> 13:26.138
No, I like being your employee.

13:27.181 --> 13:30.935
Look, the whole Lee Seo-yeon thing,
I… I take back what I said.

13:31.018 --> 13:33.771
She's not a fucking bitch.
But I don't get why she dumped you.

13:33.854 --> 13:37.024
The way I see it, you've been
in a downward spiral without her,

13:37.107 --> 13:38.984
so just do whatever it takes
to get her back.

13:39.068 --> 13:40.444
Hell, get down on your knees.

13:40.528 --> 13:41.779
Stop bothering us peasants.

13:41.862 --> 13:44.782
Ride off into the sunset with her
and live happily ever after.

13:45.282 --> 13:47.660
- I just can't.
- Can't do it? Why the hell not?

13:47.743 --> 13:50.037
With your bank account,
anything's possible!

13:50.120 --> 13:51.831
You're a moron. God.

13:56.877 --> 14:00.089
I'm so grateful that you offered
to take care of all the renovations.

14:00.589 --> 14:03.926
I kept telling my husband we should sell
that run-down building and move,

14:04.009 --> 14:06.178
but he lets his pride
get the better of him.

14:07.096 --> 14:09.765
So what's it like
having a younger husband? How is it?

14:11.267 --> 14:13.269
Hey, you know me.
I know how to keep a secret.

14:13.352 --> 14:16.772
He's never gonna find out you married
somebody else. Don't worry, all right?

14:18.649 --> 14:20.734
HAN JEONG-WON

14:26.657 --> 14:28.325
Oh, how's Jeong-won doing now?

14:29.660 --> 14:32.079
I guess you haven't heard.
He was arrested for drug--

14:32.580 --> 14:35.457
I mean, word on the street is
he allegedly got in trouble

14:35.541 --> 14:37.251
and started a fight at the label.

14:44.258 --> 14:46.552
Hi, yeah,
let's… let's have dinner tonight.

14:47.344 --> 14:48.929
I'll be there at seven o'clock.

14:50.890 --> 14:53.392
Oh, by the way,
you guys are divorced, right?

14:54.643 --> 14:57.396
I was just wondering
if you got remarried before the divorce.

14:59.523 --> 15:01.817
I'm just kidding.

15:02.985 --> 15:06.113
You think you'd be able
to live with a shell of a man?

15:07.823 --> 15:09.450
I was messing with you.

15:10.367 --> 15:12.661
Jeong-won's getting hitched.
Don't get the wrong idea.

15:13.329 --> 15:15.456
We're having dinner
'cause he's getting married.

15:15.539 --> 15:16.498
Are you for real?

15:18.167 --> 15:19.418
Wait. Who is he, uh…

15:20.085 --> 15:21.629
Oh my God! Oh my God! Oh my God!

15:22.129 --> 15:24.089
Jeong-won's getting married!
Married! Is he crazy?

15:24.173 --> 15:26.550
I guess he saw Seo-yeon's
getting remarried and lost his mind.

15:26.634 --> 15:28.928
Did you know about this? Who could it be?

15:29.011 --> 15:30.638
Maybe someone from a club.

15:30.721 --> 15:32.806
Do you think
that asshole is really on drugs?

15:39.021 --> 15:40.189
Hi, how are you?

15:43.984 --> 15:45.819
I do pills, too, from the doctor.

15:47.696 --> 15:48.530
Right.

15:52.910 --> 15:54.411
Hey, I gotta go.

15:54.495 --> 15:55.412
Okay.

16:20.562 --> 16:22.648
And your table is right over here, ma'am.

16:32.157 --> 16:33.325
It's been a while.

16:34.034 --> 16:36.161
We saw each other
at your office last week.

16:36.787 --> 16:38.205
Right, that's my point.

16:39.331 --> 16:41.625
'Cause we were supposed to
see each other every day.

16:42.126 --> 16:45.754
Well, the reason we're not doing that
isn't because we're divorced.

16:45.838 --> 16:47.297
It's 'cause I remarried.

16:47.923 --> 16:49.425
And soon, you'll do the same.

16:55.222 --> 16:56.932
Are you two ready to order?

16:57.016 --> 17:00.227
- What's the chef's special?
- It's a prix-fixe menu.

17:00.310 --> 17:03.355
The first course is
mini caprese with yukhoe and truffle oil,

17:03.439 --> 17:06.316
followed by tomato risotto
and arancini with cream cheese.

17:06.400 --> 17:08.986
The next course is beef tenderloin
with a side of prosciutto

17:09.069 --> 17:12.281
and pesto made with minced shrimp
and aralia elata.

17:12.364 --> 17:14.616
I'll do the cod steak.
Can you do no tomatoes?

17:14.700 --> 17:17.369
Someone really doesn't like tomatoes.
That's all, okay?

17:17.453 --> 17:19.705
Of course.
I'll pass that on to the kitchen.

17:30.340 --> 17:32.342
I've been carrying it around
for a week.

17:32.426 --> 17:33.969
I know you like that style.

17:40.059 --> 17:41.101
They're pretty.

17:42.686 --> 17:43.562
Try them on.

17:46.106 --> 17:47.066
I'll do that later.

17:49.026 --> 17:51.070
Your marriage will be fine. Don't worry.

17:51.653 --> 17:53.238
I don't know why you're doing this.

17:53.322 --> 17:54.573
It's just a year.

17:55.199 --> 17:57.326
Think of it like an arranged marriage.
It's easier.

17:57.409 --> 17:59.161
Seo-yeon.

18:00.370 --> 18:01.872
I don't wanna be without you.

18:02.790 --> 18:04.166
I've known you since kindergarten.

18:04.249 --> 18:06.460
I didn't study abroad
so I could be with you.

18:06.543 --> 18:09.463
You know I literally won't be able
to function without you. I'll go nuts.

18:10.047 --> 18:11.757
Come on, you've never even tried.

18:14.093 --> 18:15.427
You think it's a good…

18:18.180 --> 18:20.516
you think it's a good idea?
A temporary marriage?

18:20.599 --> 18:21.975
Look, you already signed.

18:22.059 --> 18:24.144
Yeah, because you wouldn't
see me anymore if I didn't.

18:25.979 --> 18:29.525
I know you're trying to punish me,
but you… you're taking this too far.

18:31.068 --> 18:32.027
Jeong-won.

18:33.946 --> 18:34.988
I'm punishing you?

18:45.040 --> 18:47.000
I'm the one that's being punished here.

18:47.835 --> 18:50.045
I'm alive
and sitting in front of you, right?

18:50.546 --> 18:53.006
If you don't do
the temporary marriage, Jeong-won,

18:54.007 --> 18:55.259
we're done.

19:07.771 --> 19:09.481
No, we're finished. I can go.

19:10.232 --> 19:11.608
Let's just eat at home.

19:15.279 --> 19:16.572
My husband's outside.

19:17.072 --> 19:18.198
I'm leaving, yeah?

20:38.904 --> 20:40.572
Ah shit.

20:59.716 --> 21:02.052
The number you have dialed
is not available.

21:24.783 --> 21:28.328
HAN JEONG-WON

22:02.029 --> 22:04.281
The number you have dialed
is not available.

22:04.364 --> 22:06.366
At the tone, please record your message.

22:51.036 --> 22:53.497
Jesus. Come on.
You don't have any ID on you?

22:53.580 --> 22:54.539
Really?

22:55.123 --> 22:56.083
Who's this?

22:58.001 --> 23:00.212
He tried to steal a car
and smashed a window.

23:01.338 --> 23:03.715
I was on my way back here.
I caught him in the act.

23:05.050 --> 23:06.009
Who's the owner?

23:06.093 --> 23:08.345
I've been trying to reach them,
but no answer yet.

23:09.388 --> 23:10.263
Huh.

23:12.849 --> 23:16.353
Listen, stonewalling isn't
gonna get you out of this, buddy.

23:16.436 --> 23:18.063
Wanna spend the night in a cell?

23:29.616 --> 23:30.992
Right, right, sure.

23:35.956 --> 23:36.790
Who are you?

23:37.874 --> 23:39.584
Han Jeong-won is my husband.

23:42.379 --> 23:45.632
Oh, so his name is Han Jeong-won.

23:51.263 --> 23:54.558
Uh, I just got through to the car owner.
She knew all about it.

23:55.183 --> 23:57.144
She lost her keys and told him to do it.

23:57.227 --> 23:59.271
Wait. She knew
he was smashing the window?

23:59.354 --> 24:00.981
Can we go now, Officers?

24:01.565 --> 24:02.691
Uh…

24:04.192 --> 24:06.236
- Uh…
- Honey, let's go home now.

24:38.810 --> 24:40.896
Owner said
the boat was missing in the morning,

24:40.979 --> 24:42.397
then they found it like this.

24:42.481 --> 24:44.357
That, and a local fisherman told me

24:44.441 --> 24:46.651
he thought he heard a gunshot
around one o'clock.

24:47.152 --> 24:49.196
But he didn't bother
to call the police?

24:49.905 --> 24:51.656
Maybe he thought it was a firework.

24:52.324 --> 24:54.534
- Any casings?
- Not yet.

24:55.035 --> 24:56.036
CCTV?

24:56.536 --> 24:59.206
There's one at the kayak house,
but that's it.

24:59.831 --> 25:01.166
Someone cut the wires.

25:01.958 --> 25:04.211
So there's no body,
just a trunk, huh?

25:05.921 --> 25:10.091
Sir, do… do you… you know
how much that's worth?

25:11.927 --> 25:15.305
It's over 50 million won.
Five-zero. Swear to God.

25:18.058 --> 25:20.227
It's a rare,
limited-edition designer trunk.

25:20.310 --> 25:22.229
There are only three of them in Korea.

25:24.231 --> 25:26.566
Do me a favor. Call the store,
give 'em the serial number,

25:26.650 --> 25:28.235
and find out who bought it, okay?

25:28.318 --> 25:31.112
They don't sell these to random people.
They'll have a record.

25:31.863 --> 25:33.740
But how the hell would you know that?

25:36.701 --> 25:39.037
This thing is Prada.
You got a problem with that?

25:41.289 --> 25:42.374
Is it fake?

25:43.333 --> 25:44.751
Oh, no? Sure.

25:44.834 --> 25:46.086
Okay. Get that.

26:02.894 --> 26:04.312
Should I be thanking you?

26:04.938 --> 26:07.190
Oh, no. You're working. I forgot.

26:08.316 --> 26:09.484
No need for that.

26:10.735 --> 26:13.905
Sorry, I couldn't bring my car
because they took me right to the station.

26:13.989 --> 26:15.657
I guess I'll have to take a taxi.

26:17.200 --> 26:18.785
You'll find your way, right?

26:54.654 --> 26:55.739
Let's go.

27:01.411 --> 27:02.495
Hey, isn't this my car?

27:02.579 --> 27:04.205
Yeah, get in already.

27:31.191 --> 27:34.110
So I think you owe me an explanation.
Go ahead.

27:35.862 --> 27:36.946
It was Mr. Kim.

27:38.073 --> 27:39.991
You said you didn't want arbitration.

27:45.580 --> 27:46.748
Question for you.

27:48.667 --> 27:49.584
Yeah?

27:52.671 --> 27:54.422
It's your job to get married, right?

27:59.969 --> 28:01.388
Do you enjoy your work?

28:11.690 --> 28:12.691
It depends.

28:34.587 --> 28:35.839
I'll take that one.

28:35.922 --> 28:37.716
Oh, a man with great taste!

28:37.799 --> 28:39.843
I'm sure the bride-to-be
is going to love it.

28:39.926 --> 28:41.428
I have a good eye.

28:42.011 --> 28:43.388
It's number two for me, so…

28:46.099 --> 28:48.017
- Let's do it.
- Oh, right.

28:50.812 --> 28:52.981
It looks like your ex-wife referred you.

28:54.566 --> 28:56.317
Isn't that how you get all your clients?

28:58.528 --> 29:00.363
What I'd really like to know is

29:01.030 --> 29:03.199
why you are running this kind of business?

29:04.659 --> 29:06.077
You're matchmaking on the down-low

29:06.161 --> 29:09.247
'cause the wedding stuff
isn't bringing enough cash, huh?

29:13.251 --> 29:17.505
About how long do you think your marriage
is going to last with your current wife?

29:18.882 --> 29:21.050
As our lifespans get longer and longer,

29:21.134 --> 29:24.012
we might have one partner
for a hundred years. Who knows?

29:24.721 --> 29:25.680
Pretty long.

29:26.806 --> 29:28.057
Could you do that?

29:30.560 --> 29:33.480
We're looking for
the model of a happy marriage.

29:33.980 --> 29:36.649
You could say
we're staying ahead of the curve.

29:39.652 --> 29:42.280
So consider yourself a lucky man.

30:14.854 --> 30:16.356
I figured you didn't eat.

30:16.439 --> 30:18.399
It's pine nut soup with vegetables.

30:22.153 --> 30:24.531
I'm in the empty bedroom
on the second floor.

30:24.614 --> 30:26.950
I can always move to another room
if you want.

30:27.033 --> 30:28.993
So do I refer to you as my wife?

30:30.203 --> 30:31.746
Is that the typical arrangement?

30:32.914 --> 30:33.748
Yeah.

30:36.042 --> 30:37.919
It's weird to call you my wife since

30:38.753 --> 30:40.213
our relationship is so unofficial.

30:41.005 --> 30:42.882
Well, other marriages are different.

30:42.966 --> 30:45.385
You wanted a more discrete situation.
Isn't that right?

30:49.973 --> 30:51.015
I guess.

30:51.558 --> 30:54.394
I'm going to continue our arrangement
for now, then.

30:54.477 --> 30:57.146
But I'm really not sure what I should
and shouldn't do with all this…

30:57.230 --> 30:58.648
You should check the manual.

31:01.651 --> 31:02.735
Good night.

33:39.892 --> 33:41.019
I understand.

33:43.104 --> 33:44.272
Come on, Mom.

33:50.653 --> 33:52.363
No, Mom.

33:54.741 --> 33:55.908
No, Mom.

34:00.246 --> 34:01.289
Mom.

34:38.701 --> 34:40.828
You're up a lot earlier
than I thought you'd be.

34:41.496 --> 34:43.581
You don't need to make me breakfast.

34:43.664 --> 34:45.333
I almost never eat my meals here.

34:45.416 --> 34:48.294
Well, I just thought I'd try
to do something nice for you.

34:53.049 --> 34:53.883
Sit down.

34:55.635 --> 34:57.553
Humor me. It's our first day together.

35:14.612 --> 35:18.533
So halibut has lots of collagen.
I know you really like fish.

35:19.367 --> 35:20.743
Well, there's something

35:21.661 --> 35:23.538
I like even more than fish.

35:29.127 --> 35:32.713
I'm not in the mood for that right now.
I have a weak stomach, you know.

35:34.173 --> 35:35.550
It smells a bit too fishy.

36:24.807 --> 36:26.475
Uh, once more.

37:59.026 --> 38:00.444
How long you gonna keep that here?

38:01.654 --> 38:02.738
Wait, whose is it?

38:03.239 --> 38:05.491
Well, it's not mine. Go ahead.

38:12.665 --> 38:15.126
Is this what they sent your friend
when she got stiffed?

38:15.209 --> 38:17.795
What was her name again?
Si-jeong or Bang-jeong? I forget.

38:24.093 --> 38:24.969
Ah.

38:25.594 --> 38:27.013
You know, it's not half bad.

38:27.972 --> 38:29.765
Don't let them die, okay?

38:29.849 --> 38:32.184
Well, ya know,
that's not really up to me, huh?

38:33.394 --> 38:35.646
You never know
what life's gonna throw at you.

38:36.314 --> 38:38.774
Who knows?
I might end up dying before these guys.

38:39.442 --> 38:41.444
I won't let 'em starve, that's for sure.

38:42.069 --> 38:43.696
I'll switch out their water too.

38:49.285 --> 38:51.412
Have you heard from
the punk who owns the place?

38:51.495 --> 38:54.332
He left this empty house
like a snake shedding its skin.

38:55.207 --> 38:56.876
Just remember
to take care of the fish tank.

38:56.959 --> 38:58.085
Don't touch anything.

38:59.837 --> 39:01.172
You kill him or something?

39:05.259 --> 39:07.887
I mean, it's fine by me if you did.

39:08.471 --> 39:10.222
That would make more sense.

39:10.306 --> 39:13.642
More sense than some guy going AWOL
for years just before he gets married.

39:13.726 --> 39:14.769
Basically vanishing.

39:15.269 --> 39:17.772
Yeah. You're right. I did it.

39:17.855 --> 39:20.191
Crazy bitch.
Get over him already, will ya?

39:20.775 --> 39:24.153
Just live a normal life.
Get married and have kids like everyone.

39:26.906 --> 39:28.991
Refill the coffee thing
so we don't run out.

40:00.856 --> 40:03.692
SI-JEONG

40:05.403 --> 40:06.237
Mm-hmm?

40:06.737 --> 40:08.906
Hey, In-ji, that bastard is out!

40:08.989 --> 40:10.157
Uh, who?

40:10.658 --> 40:12.493
Eom Tae-seong. Who do you think?

40:13.077 --> 40:15.621
I was doing a delivery,
and I ran into him by accident.

40:15.704 --> 40:17.206
How the hell did he get out?

40:17.706 --> 40:20.584
Wasn't he supposed to rot
in a mental hospital for life?

40:22.336 --> 40:23.879
Okay, tell me where he is.

40:32.179 --> 40:33.514
Son of a bitch. Really?

40:33.597 --> 40:37.351
Listen, don't do anything for now.
I'll look into it and call you back.

41:50.216 --> 41:53.427
Uh, I saw the earrings in the car,
through the window.

41:53.511 --> 41:55.346
I know. I heard. The police called.

41:56.972 --> 42:00.142
Right. Thanks for smoothing things out
on my behalf.

42:00.226 --> 42:03.145
I could… get you a new car?

42:14.823 --> 42:16.575
I forgot the case
'cause I put them on right away.

42:16.659 --> 42:18.035
I wasn't getting rid of them.

42:20.663 --> 42:22.289
They're beautiful. I said that.

42:25.209 --> 42:27.002
This is so embarrassing.

42:33.759 --> 42:35.219
So tell me about the first night.

42:39.056 --> 42:41.350
Oh. It was good.

42:42.643 --> 42:43.686
Glad to hear that.

42:46.146 --> 42:47.064
Mm.

42:55.239 --> 42:56.490
Doors closing.

43:12.631 --> 43:14.174
It's almost over.

43:14.258 --> 43:15.968
You're with me. You're all right.

43:19.555 --> 43:21.974
Oh, I left my keys at the office.

43:41.243 --> 43:42.453
I feel like…

43:45.205 --> 43:47.416
a dog that can't be separated
from its owner.

43:49.293 --> 43:50.794
Let's try again.

43:51.754 --> 43:53.005
We could just start all over.

43:53.088 --> 43:56.467
This whole… arrangement is stupid.

43:57.760 --> 43:58.719
Sweetheart,

43:59.762 --> 44:00.888
the thing is,

44:02.640 --> 44:05.392
I just wish you'd die already.

44:08.771 --> 44:10.189
Doors opening.

44:14.443 --> 44:15.736
Doors closing.

44:57.903 --> 44:58.862
Yeah, hello?

44:59.738 --> 45:01.782
Come on out.
You can't just sit there.

45:14.294 --> 45:15.337
You make good food?

45:17.214 --> 45:18.048
I try.

45:27.349 --> 45:29.476
Come on, now.
You don't have to overthink this.

45:29.560 --> 45:31.562
Till death do us part, happily ever after.

45:31.645 --> 45:34.148
All those vows
only last a year for us, you know.

45:42.740 --> 45:43.949
Not bad, yeah.

45:44.658 --> 45:46.160
The fish has all the taste.

45:46.702 --> 45:49.621
I used your card to buy really nice fish,
just so you know.

46:00.507 --> 46:01.967
So this is some kinda

46:03.051 --> 46:05.721
super overpriced
housemaid service or something?

46:09.683 --> 46:11.101
With sex included?

46:14.605 --> 46:17.983
If it's not, I hope you don't mind
if your husband cheats.

46:19.026 --> 46:20.360
I can't get enough action.

46:22.654 --> 46:24.156
Well, is that what you want?

47:28.846 --> 47:30.264
Is that inappropriate?

47:34.268 --> 47:35.519
We're married, aren't we?

47:43.777 --> 47:44.945
If we're…

47:50.450 --> 47:51.827
in agreement.

48:01.545 --> 48:03.422
This might take a little while, then.

48:06.592 --> 48:08.552
See, the truth is I can be kind of shy.

48:18.604 --> 48:20.105
Thanks for dinner. Oh…

48:22.274 --> 48:24.318
I guess I'm not sure I need to thank you.

48:24.902 --> 48:26.528
I mean, I haven't read the manual.

48:45.505 --> 48:46.465
Mm!

50:13.301 --> 50:16.596
…the other team have to start playing
football to get back into the game…

50:20.809 --> 50:22.310
Excuse me, uh…

50:23.687 --> 50:26.481
Oh, I'm sorry if I woke you up.
I just really have to watch this match.

50:27.774 --> 50:28.734
Do you like soccer?

50:29.276 --> 50:30.277
I don't.

50:30.861 --> 50:31.862
Baseball?

50:31.945 --> 50:34.031
Truth is, I think it's all ridiculous.

50:34.948 --> 50:36.950
Of course. Team sports aren't your thing.

50:38.452 --> 50:41.038
Buy a TV for your room.
As many as you want.

50:45.292 --> 50:46.793
Does it bother you that much?

50:46.877 --> 50:49.880
Your "system" clearly isn't all
it's cracked up to be, is it?

50:49.963 --> 50:51.506
I mean, don't you know I have insomnia?

50:51.590 --> 50:53.383
Pretty easy to tell.
I'm taking tons of pills.

50:53.967 --> 50:55.093
I read your file.

50:56.261 --> 50:59.222
And I'm aware that you can't sleep
and you're dependent on drugs.

50:59.306 --> 51:01.183
You won't be out anytime soon,
so sit down.

51:01.266 --> 51:02.476
- Stop it.
- Who knows?

51:02.559 --> 51:05.187
Maybe you'll fall asleep
if you watch something boring on TV.

51:06.313 --> 51:07.147
Look, In-ji…

51:07.230 --> 51:08.106
Yes, boo?

51:11.026 --> 51:11.943
Want a drink?

51:12.652 --> 51:14.112
I'll get you a cold one.

51:15.530 --> 51:16.490
Wait right here.

52:01.701 --> 52:05.413
Well, you have no brains whatsoever.
At least you're pretty spry and quick.

52:05.914 --> 52:07.833
You know, you can live somewhere else.

52:09.251 --> 52:11.128
If you don't have a place,
tell me what you want.

52:11.211 --> 52:13.797
An apartment. A brand-new house.
I won't say anything.

52:13.880 --> 52:14.840
Let's just

52:16.341 --> 52:18.510
let the year go by
as quickly and quietly as poss--

52:18.593 --> 52:19.553
Jeong-won.

52:26.184 --> 52:27.394
You're being so coy.

52:29.896 --> 52:32.107
I don't need to lure you in

52:33.775 --> 52:36.611
to get you to feel comfortable
around me, do I?

52:39.906 --> 52:41.491
We're together. It's just us.

52:41.575 --> 52:42.742
You know you

52:43.702 --> 52:45.245
can just be yourself.

55:05.802 --> 55:09.431
So how are you related to
the owner of the trunk to my left?

55:12.684 --> 55:13.893
I'm her husband.
